    "title": "Bodø/Glimt Defeats Inter Milan in Champions League Playoff",
    "text": "• Bodø/Glimt defeated Inter Milan 3-1 in the first leg of their Champions League playoff.\n• The match took place on Wednesday.\n• Inter Milan was the Champions League runner-up.\n• Bodø/Glimt had previously defeated Manchester City at home and Atletico Madrid away.\n• Bodø/Glimt is located north of the Arctic Circle.\n• Inter Milan was the Serie A leader.\n• Sondre Brunstad Fet scored for Bodø/Glimt in the 20th minute.\n• Pio Esposito scored for Inter Milan 10 minutes later.\n• Jens Petter Hauge scored for Bodø/Glimt in the 61st minute.\n• Kasper Høgh scored for Bodø/Glimt three minutes later.\n• The return leg is scheduled for next Tuesday.\n• The article was published on February 19, 2026, at 10:38 IST.",
    "summary": "The Norwegian outsider has been the surprise story of this season’s competition after beating Manchester City at home and Atletico Madrid away to make the playoffs. Serie A leader Inter was seeking a seventh straight win in all competitions but fell behind in the 20th minute when midfielder Sondre Brunstad Fet netted with a neat finish. Although burly striker Pio Esposito equalized with an opportunist finish 10 minutes later, the home side picked off Inter with two goals in quick succession in the second half.",
